"# aos-exec: run one entry\n\nThe base of everything: daemons, loops, fsm cells and tool calls all run through it. Use it by hand to try a function or tool once.\n\n```sh\naos-exec hello a b                        # hello/_entry with args a b\n# ws=/tmp/w stack=/tmp/w/.stack/ args=a b\naos-exec --ws /work --stack /tmp/st hello\naos-exec p.json#/x                        # an instruction inside a JSON file\naos-exec $AOS_HOME/lib/base/math --expr '6*7'   # a lib tool; flags fill its JSON input\n# 42\n```\n\nIt sets `AOS_WS` (`--ws`, else the outer `$AOS_WS`, else the current folder) and `AOS_STACK` (`--stack`, else the outer one, else `WS/.stack/`), reads `.env` (`--dotenv-override` lets it win over set variables) and runs the entry. The exit code is the entry's. `EntryMissing`: no such path. `EntryBad`: not runnable; a loop config needs aos-loop, and an fsm table needs `\"_entry\": [\"aos-fsm\", {\"$env\": \"AOS_CF\"}]`.\n"
